r boots cleanly.\n\n## How to Use\n\n```bash\ncd inference\nsource .venv/bin/activate\n\n# Run server\nuvicorn main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\n\n### Generate an image\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \"http://localhost:8000/inference/image?model=flux\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: your_api_key\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"prompt\": \"a cat in space wearing an astronaut helmet\",\n    \"width\": 1024,\n    \"height\": 1024,\n    \"seed\": 42,\n    \"negative_prompt\": \"blurry\",\n    \"nologo\": true,\n    \"private\": false\n  }'\n```\n\n### Response\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"image_url\": \"https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/a%20cat%20in%20space...\",\n    \"model\": \"flux\",\n    \"prompt\": \"a cat in space wearing an astronaut helmet\",\n    \"width\": 1024,\n    \"height\": 1024,\n    \"seed\": 42,\n    \"metadata\": { \"nologo\": true, \"provider\": \"pollinations\" }\n  },\n  \"error\": null\n}\n```\n\n### List available models\n```bash\ncurl \"http://localhost:8000/inference/models\"\n```\n\n## Key Architecture Points\n\n- **Single `InferenceRelay` class** routes all requests — just call `relay.route(task_type, model, payload, api_key)`\n- **Provider-per-class** — each provider defines its own `task_type`, `supported_models`, `request_model`, `generate()`, and `format_output()`\n- **Adding a new provider**: subclass `BaseProvider`, implement required methods, register in `registry.py` — the relay auto-discovers it\n- **API keys** passed via `X-API-Key` header, forwarded to providers that need them\n- **Everything configurable** in `.env` — copy `.env.example` to `.env` and customize\n- **Video, text, enhancement** are stubbed with request/response models and routes, ready for providers to be added\n\nAll `.env` variables, provider configs, and model defaults are externalized and configurable.","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}

